{# Parser-level whitelist (s02-enrich) for the homepage dashboard's own polling
   API. The browser tab polls /api/docker/status/<service>/<instance> once per
   tile, every few seconds, for as long as the dashboard is open.

   Any event that takes every container down at once — a dockerd restart, most
   notably — leaves traefik running with an empty router table, so it answers
   404 to each of those polls. One open dashboard then produces a burst of
   unique 4xx URIs from the viewer's own IP, which is exactly the shape of
   crowdsecurity/http-probing: 11 events in 4.9s was enough to self-ban, and
   because the bouncer filters INPUT while docker-published ports bypass it,
   the ban took out SSH and left the web reachable.

   Deliberately NOT scoped by traefik_router_name the way ha-hls-whitelist is:
   during the outage that matters here no router matched at all, so the log
   carries "-" in that field and a router-scoped expression would miss the very
   events it is meant to cover. /api/docker/ is served by nothing else on this
   host, and it is not an endpoint worth probing for, so a path-only scope costs
   no real detection.

   Field name matches ha-hls-whitelist.yaml.j2, verified with
   `cscli explain --type traefik`. #}
name: local/homepage-api-whitelist
description: "Whitelist the homepage dashboard's own polling API (benign 404 bursts while backends are down)"
whitelist:
  reason: "homepage dashboard status polling — not http-probing"
  expression:
    - evt.Parsed.request startsWith '/api/docker/'
